'''Mur Pano''', or simply '''Pano''', is an [[Austronesian language]] spoken by about three quarters of the thousand inhabitants of Mur village on the north coast of [[Madang Province]], [[Papua New Guinea]].   The other quarter of the population speaks [[Molet language|Molet]] as their primary language.

